## Git Version
**Syntax:**
```
git --version
```
Example:
git version 2.55.0.windows.5

## Git Clone
**Purpose:** Clone a remote repository to the local machine.

Steps
Open the repository on GitHub.
Click Code.
Select HTTPS.
Copy the repository URL.
Run the git clone command in Git Bash.

**Syntax:**
```
git clone <repository-URL>
```
Example:
git clone https://github.com/gopikadeviga/git-journey.git

This creates a local copy of the git-journey repository on your computer.

## Git status
**Purpose:** Check the current status of the working directory and see what changes have been made.

**Syntax:**
```
git status
```




